module TokenDisbursement where 
-- 1. TokenWallet Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Represents an account-based token wallet that holds a borrower's
--   disbursed loan balance. Models the bank account into which approved
--   loan funds are deposited. The issuer credits funds on disbursement;
--   the owner debits funds when spending or repaying. The separation of
--   credit (issuer-controlled) and debit (owner-controlled) mirrors the
--   real-world model where a bank deposits funds into a customer account
--   and the customer controls outgoing transactions.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: issuer, owner
--   Both parties co-sign the wallet because it represents a custodial
--   relationship — the issuer holds and manages the funds, the owner
--   has the right to the balance. Dual signatories prevent either party
--   from unilaterally creating or closing the account. The issuer cannot
--   open a wallet on behalf of a borrower without their authorization,
--   and the owner cannot self-issue a funded wallet.
--
-- OBSERVERS: none
--   No third-party observers. The wallet balance is private to the
--   account holder and the issuing institution. This reflects standard
--   bank account confidentiality — account balances are not visible to
--   other parties absent a legal order.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   GDPR Article 5(1)(c) — data minimization. The wallet is visible only
--   to issuer and owner; no other party can observe the borrower's balance.
--   CFPB Regulation Z — the issuer-controlled Credit choice ensures funds
--   can only be added by the lending institution as part of an approved
--   disbursement, not self-credited by the borrower.
--
-- MIGRATION NOTE:
--   This template uses a pattern that would benefit from contract keys in
--   DAML 2.x. In DAML 3.x LF 2.1, contract keys are not supported. The
--   current implementation relies on off-ledger tracking of contract IDs.
--   A future refactor should evaluate the Participant Query Store as the
--   recommended replacement pattern.
template TokenWallet -- Created a Token Wallet account, so the funds will be Deposited and Transfered from here.
  with 
    owner : Party
    issuer  : Party
    tokenAmount  : Decimal -- This is the Token balance of the wallet
  where
    signatory issuer, owner  -- Both parties have access to the TokenWallet

    choice Credit : ContractId  TokenWallet -- Add funds to the TokenWallet
      with
        amount : Decimal 
      controller  issuer
        do 
        assertMsg "The amount should be positive" (amount > 0.0) -- Make sures the amount entered is Positive.
        create this with 
          tokenAmount = tokenAmount + amount -- Updates the Account Balance by adding the amount 

    choice Debit : ContractId TokenWallet -- Deducts amount from the TokenWallet
      with 
        amount : Decimal 
      controller  owner
        do 
        assertMsg "Insufficient balance" (amount <= tokenAmount) -- Make sures the requested amount is in the account.
        assertMsg " Sent amount should be greater than zero" ( amount > 0.0) -- Make sure the amount is more than zero.
        create this with 
          tokenAmount = tokenAmount - amount -- Deducts the funds from thwe account and updates
                 
-- 2. Loan Limit Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Represents the bank's credit concentration control — a bank-wide
--   lending capacity that decrements with each approved loan and tracks
--   how much the institution can still lend across all active borrowers.
--   This is distinct from the per-borrower limit governed by 12 USC 84
--   (OCC legal lending limit, capped at 15% of unimpaired capital per
--   single borrower). The totalLimit here models an aggregate portfolio
--   constraint: the bank has a total pool of lendable funds, and each
--   approval draws from that pool until it is exhausted.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: issuer
--   The bank is the sole signatory because lending capacity is an
--   institutional asset that the bank alone controls. Borrowers have no
--   legal claim over the bank's internal capital allocation decisions.
--   The bank sets, updates, and enforces its own concentration limits
--   as a matter of internal credit policy.
--
-- OBSERVERS: none
--   No observers. The bank's total lending capacity and internal limits
--   are proprietary credit risk data. Exposing this to borrowers would
--   reveal how much aggregate lending headroom the bank has — competitively
--   sensitive information that borrowers have no right to see.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   FDIC Interagency Guidelines for Credit Concentration Risk — the
--   totalLimit field implements a portfolio-level concentration control,
--   consistent with supervisory guidance that banks maintain internal
--   limits on credit concentrations relative to capital.
--   12 USC 84 (OCC Legal Lending Limit) — acknowledged as the statutory
--   per-borrower cap; the totalLimit here models the bank's internal
--   aggregate capacity, a complementary but distinct control.
template LoanLimit -- Based on the Individuals Income
  with 
    issuer : Party
    --salary : Decimal -- Asking Income
    loanLimit : Decimal  -- Considered as Limit for a individual person
    loanRequested : Decimal --  Considered as a Requested loan amount by a person
    totalLimit : Decimal --  Total Predefined amount set by the Bank
  where
    signatory issuer  -- only bank can control the limits

    choice CheckLimit : ContractId LoanLimit -- Updates the loanLimit and totalLimit
      with
        loanAmount : Decimal
        salary : Decimal
      controller issuer -- Bank is the Controller
        do
        assertMsg "The amount should be 25% of the Salary" (loanAmount <= 0.25 * salary) -- checking the requested loan is 25% of the salary
        assertMsg "Loan Limit Exceded" (loanAmount <= totalLimit) -- checking the requested amount is under the total loan limit
        create this with
          loanLimit = 0.25 * salary --  Gives the Loanlimit amount for a individual
          totalLimit = totalLimit - loanAmount -- Updates the totalLimit after each LoanApproval
          loanRequested = loanAmount  -- Updated with the loan amount

-- 3. LoanRequest Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Extends the basic loan application from Module 1 with income-based
--   eligibility verification and integration with the bank's lending
--   capacity limit. The borrower provides their salary alongside the
--   requested amount; the ApproveRequest choice validates that the
--   loan does not exceed 25% of salary and exercises the LoanLimit's
--   CheckLimit choice to atomically deduct from the bank's total pool.
--   This implements the CFPB Ability-to-Repay principle at the contract
--   level — the eligibility check cannot be skipped or overridden by
--   application code.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: owner (borrower)
--   The borrower signs the request, committing their stated income and
--   requested amount to the ledger. This creates an on-ledger record
--   of the borrower's representations at time of application, which
--   supports the bank's documentation obligation under BSA CIP rules.
--
-- OBSERVERS: issuer (bank)
--   The bank observes the request to evaluate and exercise the approval
--   choice. It does not co-sign the request because it has not yet made
--   a credit decision — observation without signature reflects the bank's
--   review role at this stage.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   CFPB Ability-to-Repay (Regulation Z) — the 25% debt-to-income check
--   inside ApproveRequest enforces income-based lending eligibility as a
--   contract assertion. If the borrower's stated salary does not support
--   the requested amount, the choice fails at the interpreter level.
--   BSA Section 1020.220 (Customer Identification Program) — the owner
--   party represents the identified loan applicant; in a production
--   system this would be linked to a verified identity record.
template LoanRequest -- Borrower requests the loan
  with 
    loanLimitCid : ContractId LoanLimit   -- checking the Loan LoanLimit
    issuer : Party 
    owner : Party
    salary : Decimal -- Takes salary as input
    loanAmount : Decimal -- Takes input as loanAmount
    
  where
    signatory owner  -- owner requests the loan so owner is signatory
    observer issuer  -- issuer acts as observer
    
    choice ApproveRequest : ContractId Loan -- Choice to accept the Request
      controller issuer   -- Only issuer can perform this action 
      do
      -- Validating the loan limit by taking input salary and loan amount calculating with loan limit template
      let isValid = loanAmount <= 0.25 * salary 
      if isValid then do
      _ <- exercise loanLimitCid CheckLimit with 
        salary = salary
        loanAmount = loanAmount  
      create Loan with   -- creates loan if loan request is under the loan limit
        issuer 
        owner 
        loanAmount = loanAmount
        disbursedAmount = 0.0
        status = "Approved" -- If Approved status Changed to Approved
      else 
       create Loan with  -- if the loan request amount is over the loanlimit
         issuer
         owner 
         loanAmount = loanAmount
         disbursedAmount = 0.0
         status = "Rejected"  -- Updates status as rejected

-- 4. Loan Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Extends the Module 1 Loan contract with disbursement tracking.
--   Adds disbursedAmount to record how much of the approved loan has
--   been released into the borrower's wallet. The Disburse choice allows
--   the bank to release funds incrementally — each tranche is validated
--   against the approved loanAmount before the Credit choice on the
--   TokenWallet is exercised. This models the real-world practice of
--   staged loan disbursement, common in construction loans, revolving
--   credit facilities, and milestone-based lending.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: issuer, owner
--   Both parties co-sign the loan agreement. The issuer's signature
--   represents the bank's credit decision and commitment to disburse
--   up to the approved amount. The owner's signature represents the
--   borrower's acceptance of the loan terms. Neither can unilaterally
--   modify the loan record after creation.
--
-- OBSERVERS: none
--   No third-party observers. Loan terms and disbursement status are
--   private to the contracting parties. The borrower's outstanding
--   balance is not visible to other borrowers or external parties.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   CFPB Regulation Z — the Disburse choice assertion
--   (disbursedAmount + disAmount <= loanAmount) enforces that total
--   disbursement never exceeds the approved credit limit. This is a
--   contract-level control that cannot be bypassed by repeated calls.
--   FDIC Credit Concentration Guidelines — the disbursedAmount field
--   provides on-ledger visibility into actual funds released, supporting
--   the bank's internal exposure tracking against the LoanLimit contract.
template Loan  -- This is a Loan Template created after the Request Approved or Rejected
  with
    issuer : Party
    owner : Party
    loanAmount : Decimal
    disbursedAmount: Decimal
    status : Text
  where
    signatory issuer, owner  -- agreement between issuer and owner

    choice Disburse : ContractId Loan  -- disbursing the approved amount into toekn wallet
      with
        disAmount : Decimal 
        tokenWalletCid : ContractId TokenWallet  -- tokenwallet contract address
      controller issuer
      do
        assertMsg "Disbursement Amount must be positive" (disAmount > 0.0)   -- checking if the disburse amount is greater than zero
        assertMsg "Disbuesement exceds remaining limit" (disbursedAmount + disAmount <= loanAmount)  -- ensuring disbursed amount doesnt exceed the loan amount
        _ <- exercise tokenWalletCid Credit with amount = disAmount   -- exercisng the credit choice in tokenwallet
        create this with 
         disbursedAmount = disbursedAmount + disAmount -- updating the disburse amount in loan contract
      
    





